    "anchor": "PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 Appendix B16, inherited B11/B15 and first corrector f_V=V.adjoint f_perp; exact original finite-dimensional C2/two Hessian/positive capped eta inputs.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
    "original_text": "Attributed mathematical restatement; exact selected boundary, with internally completed adapters.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted. Define the actual closed conditional-mean-zero space H_perp=ker P in L²(J;ℝ), with its inherited complete Hilbert structure; this is not merely the globally zero-mean joint space. There exists B_0:H_P^0→H_perp whose inclusion equals B i_0. There exists V_0:H_P^0→H_perp with V_0=B_0 Inv, B_0=V_0 Γ_0, V_0* V_0=I and ‖V_0 f‖=‖f‖ for every f∈H_P^0. All these objects and identities are conclusions from the same original inputs. The genuine original-input consumer proves B_0* g=Γ_0 V_0* g, ‖V_0* g‖≤‖g‖ and V_0*(g−V_0 V_0* g)=0 for every g∈H_perp. No surjectivity onto H_perp or equality V_0 V_0*=I on that entire space is claimed.\nSource anchor: PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 Appendix B16, inherited B11/B15 and first corrector f_V=V.adjoint f_perp; exact original finite-dimensional C2/two Hessian/positive capped eta inputs.",
    "text_sha256": "85b4db07b01b10fa9fc4c26307f99993bb2b2dc8375ed3d1198518464c803470"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.PolarIsometry.actual_centered_polar_isometry",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/PolarIsometry.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    let Λ := J.map (fun p : E × E => (p.2,(2 : ℝ) • p.1-p.2))\n    let F := fun p : E × E => (p.1,(2 : ℝ) • p.1-p.2)\n    let mY := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n    letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n    letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) :=\n      ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n    let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n    let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n      HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n    let hp : MeasurePreserving (Prod.snd : E × E → E) J ν := ⟨measurable_snd,rfl⟩\n    let M : Lp ℝ 2 ν →ₗᵢ[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J := Lp.compMeasurePreservingₗᵢ ℝ Prod.snd hp\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure J ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n    HP = P.toLinearMap.range ∧\n    (∀ f : HP, P (f : Lp ℝ 2 J) = f) ∧\n    ∃ S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted\n        (fun x => -V ((1/2 : ℝ) • (y+x)) - ‖y-x‖^2/(8*η))) ∧\n      Λ.IsCondKernel S ∧ Λ.fst = ν ∧ Λ.snd = ν ∧\n      ∃ e : Lp ℝ 2 ν ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] HP,\n        (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, (e u : Lp ℝ 2 J) = M u) ∧\n        ∃ U : Lp ℝ 2 J →ₗᵢ[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J,\n          (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J, (U g : E × E → ℝ) =ᵐ[J] g ∘ F) ∧\n          Function.Involutive U ∧ IsSelfAdjoint U.toContinuousLinearMap ∧\n          ∃ T : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n            IsSelfAdjoint T ∧\n            (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n              ‖T u‖ ≤ ‖u‖ ∧\n              (T u : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν] (fun y => ∫ x, u x ∂S y) ∧\n              (∫ y, T u y ∂ν) = ∫ y, u y ∂ν) ∧\n            let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP :=\n              HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n            let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n              (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n            A = e.conjStarAlgEquiv T ∧ IsSelfAdjoint A ∧\n            (∀ f : HP, ‖A f‖ ≤ ‖f‖) ∧\n            (∀ f : HP, P (B f) = 0) ∧\n            ∃ Γ : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n              Γ.IsPositive ∧ Γ*Γ=(1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T ∧\n              let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n              ΓP.IsPositive ∧ ΓP*ΓP=(1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A ∧\n              B.adjoint ∘L B = ΓP*ΓP ∧\n              ∃ q : Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n                (q : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν] (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) ∧ T q = q ∧\n                (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, inner ℝ q u = ∫ y, u y ∂ν) ∧\n                let qP : HP := e q\n                let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n                letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n                letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n                letI : CompleteSpace HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n                let γ : ℝ := 2*Real.sqrt ((α : ℝ)*η)/(1+(α : ℝ)*η)\n                (∀ f : HP, f ∈ HP0 ↔ (∫ y, (e.symm f) y ∂ν) = 0) ∧\n                ΓP qP = 0 ∧ 0 < γ ∧\n                ∃ ΓP0 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0,\n                  (∀ f : HP0, (ΓP0 f : HP) = ΓP (f : HP)) ∧\n                  ΓP0.IsPositive ∧ (ΓP0-γ • (1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0)).IsPositive ∧\n                  IsUnit ΓP0 ∧\n                  ∃ Inv : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0,\n                    Inv*ΓP0=(1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0) ∧\n                    ΓP0*Inv=(1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0) ∧ ‖Inv‖ ≤ 1/γ ∧\n                    let Hperp := P.ker\n                    letI : NormedAddCommGroup Hperp := Hperp.normedAddCommGroup\n                    letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ Hperp := Hperp.innerProductSpace\n                    letI : CompleteSpace Hperp := P.isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n                    ∃ B0 : HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp,\n                      (∀ f : HP0, (B0 f : Lp ℝ 2 J) = B (f : HP)) ∧\n                      ∃ V0 : HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp,\n                        V0 = B0 ∘L Inv ∧ B0 = V0 ∘L ΓP0 ∧\n                        V0.adjoint ∘L V0 = (1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0) ∧\n                        (∀ f : HP0, ‖V0 f‖ = ‖f‖)",
    "statement_sha256": "b600b71aa741c7b536936378554c73115e2c88b484625586040685166978a7e7",
