      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted. Define the actual closed conditional-mean-zero space H_perp=ker P in L²(J;ℝ), with its inherited complete Hilbert structure; this is not merely the globally zero-mean joint space. There exists B_0:H_P^0→H_perp whose inclusion equals B i_0. There exists V_0:H_P^0→H_perp with V_0=B_0 Inv, B_0=V_0 Γ_0, V_0* V_0=I and ‖V_0 f‖=‖f‖ for every f∈H_P^0. All these objects and identities are conclusions from the same original inputs. The genuine original-input consumer proves B_0* g=Γ_0 V_0* g, ‖V_0* g‖≤‖g‖ and V_0*(g−V_0 V_0* g)=0 for every g∈H_perp. No surjectivity onto H_perp or equality V_0 V_0*=I on that entire space is claimed.",
      "formula": "\\mathfrak H_\\perp=\\ker P,\\quad V_0=B_0\\Gamma_0^{-1},\\quad B_0=V_0\\Gamma_0,\\quad V_0^*V_0=I;\\quad B_0^*g=\\Gamma_0V_0^*g,\\quad\\|V_0^*g\\|\\le\\|g\\|,\\quad V_0^*(I-V_0V_0^*)g=0.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Restrict actual leakage to the exact closed conditional kernel",
          "text": "Reuse the same accepted actual laws, normalized kernel, reflection, macroscopic equivalence, centered root and bounded inverse. Since PB=0, codRestrict produces B_0 with codomain ker P. The centered domain and conditional kernel inherit completeness internally; no range or completeness premise is supplied.",
          "formula": "B_0:H_P^0\\to\\ker P,\\quad i_\\perp B_0=B i_0,\\quad PB i_0=0.",
          "lean": "  classical\n  dsimp only\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) := ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP := HP.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP := HP.innerProductSpace\n  let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hBase := AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.CenteredRootOrderInverse.actual_centered_root_order_inverse\n    (E:=E) (V:=V) (α:=α) (β:=β) (η:=η) hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  dsimp only at hBase\n  rcases hBase with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,\n      T,hTs,hAll,hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,\n      q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,\n      Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv⟩\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP := HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  let qP : HP := e q\n  let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  let Hperp := P.ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup Hperp := Hperp.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ Hperp := Hperp.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace Hperp := P.isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  let B0 : HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp :=\n    (B ∘L HP0.subtypeL).codRestrict Hperp (by intro f; exact hPB (f : HP))\n  have hB0 (f : HP0) : (B0 f : Lp ℝ 2 J)=B (f : HP) := rfl\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY excerpt; preceding exact local definitions and derived facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/PolarIsometry.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "0bfdb984537dcef74dd4654cc0d23cf6515d524a3ce843f544c03c5e513127fe",
            "start_line": 92,
            "end_line": 129,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "5e2c9118e2d313f937bab617868d379c690e68e2ca19ec1d779dbec3b1eab051"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Normalize by the same centered inverse",
          "text": "Set V_0=B_0 Inv. The SAME Gram equality B*B=Γ_P² and positivity give ‖B i_0 u‖=‖Γ_P i_0 u‖. The exact restricted-root relation and Γ_0 Inv=I turn this into ‖V_0 f‖=‖f‖ for every centered f.",
          "formula": "\\|V_0f\\|=\\|B i_0\\mathrm{Inv}f\\|=\\|\\Gamma_0\\mathrm{Inv}f\\|=\\|f\\|.",
          "lean": "  let V0 : HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp := B0 ∘L Inv\n  have hGramLocal : B.adjoint ∘L B=ΓP*ΓP := hGram\n  have hPosLocal : ΓP.IsPositive := hΓP\n  have hVnorm (f : HP0) : ‖V0 f‖=‖f‖ := by\n    let g : HP0 := Inv f\n    have hg : ΓP0 g=f := congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C f) hRight\n    have hb := B.apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_right (g : HP)\n    have hr := ΓP.apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_right (g : HP)\n    rw [hGramLocal] at hb\n    rw [hPosLocal.isSelfAdjoint.adjoint_eq] at hr\n    have hNorm : ‖B (g : HP)‖=‖ΓP (g : HP)‖ :=\n      (sq_eq_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _)).mp (hb.trans hr.symm)\n    calc\n      ‖V0 f‖=‖B (g : HP)‖ := rfl\n      _ = ‖ΓP (g : HP)‖ := hNorm\n      _ = ‖ΓP0 g‖ := congrArg (fun z : HP => ‖z‖) (hΓP0 g).symm\n      _ = ‖f‖ := congrArg (fun z : HP0 => ‖z‖) hg\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY excerpt; preceding exact local definitions and derived facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/PolarIsometry.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "0bfdb984537dcef74dd4654cc0d23cf6515d524a3ce843f544c03c5e513127fe",
            "start_line": 130,
            "end_line": 146,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "f6f0f1189e3f6602194cabdd91587641ee2b3491a11fc5da28a3ba3cce0cfcda"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove factorization and the isometric adjoint identity",
          "text": "The other cancellation Inv Γ_0=I gives B_0=V_0 Γ_0 by application to each vector. Norm preservation gives V_0*V_0=I on H_P^0. It does not make V_0 onto ker P.",
          "formula": "B_0=V_0\\Gamma_0,\\quad V_0^*V_0=I_{H_P^0}.",
          "lean": "  have hFactor : B0=V0 ∘L ΓP0 := by\n    apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n    intro f\n    change B0 f=B0 (Inv (ΓP0 f))\n    have hf : Inv (ΓP0 f)=f := congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C f) hLeft\n    rw [hf]\n  have hVadj : V0.adjoint ∘L V0=(1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0) :=\n    (ContinuousLinearMap.norm_map_iff_adjoint_comp_self V0).mp hVnorm\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY excerpt; preceding exact local definitions and derived facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/PolarIsometry.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "0bfdb984537dcef74dd4654cc0d23cf6515d524a3ce843f544c03c5e513127fe",
            "start_line": 147,
            "end_line": 154,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "a1612daca9102530a6ae2bf904e72b415cf94918baac0cfae6203d18fbb6ed81"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Consume the factorization in the actual adjoint corrector",
          "text": "The Test starts from the original potential, Hessian and step inputs and extracts these same witnesses. Taking adjoints of B_0=V_0 Γ_0 and using the positivity, hence selfadjointness, of Γ_0 gives the exact first-corrector action.",
          "formula": "B_0^*=\\Gamma_0 V_0^*,\\quad f_V=V_0^*f_\\perp.",
          "lean": "  have hBAdj : B0.adjoint=ΓP0 ∘L V0.adjoint := by\n    calc\n      B0.adjoint = (V0 ∘L ΓP0).adjoint :=\n        congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp => C.adjoint) hFactor\n      _ = ΓP0.adjoint ∘L V0.adjoint := ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_comp V0 ΓP0\n      _ = ΓP0 ∘L V0.adjoint :=\n        congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C ∘L V0.adjoint)\n          hPosLocal.isSelfAdjoint.adjoint_eq\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY excerpt; preceding exact local definitions and derived facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "Tests/ProximalBPSPolarIsometry.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "e7a2a9ffadd89911d356f076aebbfe42fa0f78c137aef1a6d50278778e327513",
            "start_line": 133,
            "end_line": 140,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "af5a8f82a43731c923ca14260186088edabc4d0c8b3673d822ae8147a85607cb"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Retain contraction and the orthogonal residual",
          "text": "Norm preservation bounds ‖V_0‖≤1, hence ‖V_0*‖≤1, including the zero-dimensional case. Evaluating V_0*V_0=I at V_0*g proves that the residual g−V_0V_0*g is annihilated by V_0*. The Test does not replace contraction by norm equality on all ker P.",
          "formula": "\\|V_0^*g\\|\\le\\|g\\|,\\quad V_0^*(g-V_0V_0^*g)=0.",
          "lean": "  have hNormV : ‖V0‖ ≤ (1 : ℝ) :=\n    ContinuousLinearMap.opNorm_le_bound _ zero_le_one (by intro f; rw [hVnorm f,one_mul])\n  have hNormAdj : ‖V0.adjoint‖ ≤ (1 : ℝ) :=\n    (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint.norm_map V0).trans_le hNormV\n  refine ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,T,hTs,hAll,\n    hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,\n    ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv,B0,hB0,V0,hVdef,\n    hFactor,hVadj,hVnorm,?_,?_,?_⟩\n  · intro g\n    exact congrArg (fun C : Hperp →L[ℝ] HP0 => C g) hBAdj\n  · intro g\n    calc\n      ‖V0.adjoint g‖ ≤ ‖V0.adjoint‖*‖g‖ := V0.adjoint.le_opNorm g\n      _ ≤ 1*‖g‖ := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hNormAdj (norm_nonneg _)\n      _ = ‖g‖ := one_mul _\n  · intro g\n    have hf : V0.adjoint (V0 (V0.adjoint g))=V0.adjoint g :=\n      congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C (V0.adjoint g)) hVadj\n    exact (map_sub V0.adjoint g (V0 (V0.adjoint g))).trans (sub_eq_zero.mpr hf.symm)\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY excerpt; preceding exact local definitions and derived facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "Tests/ProximalBPSPolarIsometry.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "e7a2a9ffadd89911d356f076aebbfe42fa0f78c137aef1a6d50278778e327513",
            "start_line": 141,
            "end_line": 159,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "a4eadd7064d4cbbbe1943fcd47549752e2a54be5eaf3d3c305fb0129e8db74fc"
          }
